# DclawOS user-session dconf profile.
#
# Debian ships no /etc/dconf/profile/user. Without this file dconf falls
# back to a user-db-only profile and SILENTLY IGNORES every system database,
# so /etc/dconf/db/local.d/00-dclawos-gnome (WhiteSur GTK/icon/cursor theme,
# enabled extensions incl. dash-to-dock/ding/user-theme, dock favorites,
# input-source defaults) would never take effect on the desktop -- while the
# GDM greeter (which has its own profile with system-db:gdm) looked fine.
# That is exactly the "登录页有主题、桌面没主题、扩展都没启用" symptom.
#
# Same lesson as the greeter profile: the system-db line is what makes the
# keyfile below it visible. Keep user-db first so user overrides still win.
user-db:user
system-db:local
